# Shellcheck config for the harness (spec 004 T-132).
#
# The CI shellcheck-on-hooks gate (harness-validate.yml, ci.yml lint.sh) runs at
# default severity and failed on a set of style-class diagnostics that are
# intentional in these hooks. We disable ONLY the cosmetic/false-positive codes
# repo-wide and FIX the substantive ones in the hooks themselves (SC1083 git
# rev-syntax quoting, SC2295 prefix-strip quoting in the security guards, SC2034
# unused vars). Anything not listed here still fails the gate.
#
# Disabled, with rationale:
#   SC2012 — "use find instead of ls": these `ls` uses are over known-safe,
#            alnum-named state files; find would be heavier for no benefit.
#   SC2011 — same family (ls | xargs) on controlled inputs.
#   SC1091 — "can't follow sourced file": the libs ARE present at runtime; the
#            linter just can't resolve the relative path statically.
#   SC2016 — "expr won't expand in single quotes": intentional — these are
#            literal patterns/regex fed to grep/awk, not meant to expand.
#   SC2221/SC2222 — overlapping case patterns: verified benign (the broader
#            pattern subsumes a redundant narrower one routing to the same arm).
disable=SC2012,SC2011,SC1091,SC2016,SC2221,SC2222
